```
@id("close-workorder-main-with-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"get_workorder"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.approval_outcome: "SIGNED_OFF",
    output.approver_type: "OPERATOR"
  }
};

// get_workorder must be permitted itself, or its response is never recorded
// and the close policy above could never be satisfied.
@id("allow-get-workorder")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_workorder", resource);

@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_failure_codes",
    Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval"
  ],
  resource
);
```

The close policy requires a `get_workorder` response recorded within the last hour. That response must be for the same `wonum` and `site_id` as the close request, and must show `approval_outcome` `SIGNED_OFF` and `approver_type` `OPERATOR`. Refused (`DECLINED`) or waiting (`QUEUED`) approvals do not match. Neither do approvals by `BOT` or `SCHEDULER`, so the agent cannot approve its own work. Only a `::response` event matches, so a failed or denied lookup confirms nothing.

I used `get_workorder` as the evidence source rather than `authority_get_approval`. Its output enums are declared in the schema, whereas `authority_get_approval` returns free-form strings and I don't know what values mean "approved" or "human". That tool is still allowed as a read-only lookup, but a call to it does not satisfy the close policy.

The close policy also requires `site_id == "MAIN"`. There is no permit for `approve_workorder`, `generate_work_order`, `update_workorder`, `assign_technician` or `cancel_workorder`, so all of those are denied by default.

I did not test that the `output.approval_outcome: "SIGNED_OFF"` literal matches against the enum-typed output field.
